<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.8.0</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.8.0 -- a full accessibility audit of the UI Kit (58 findings, adversarially verified) plus an EditFile addition.

BREAKING
- IMessageService/INotificationService gain Pause(Guid)/Resume(Guid) (WCAG 2.2.1 toast auto-dismiss control). Source break only for a hand-written implementation of either interface -- the built-in MessageService/NotificationService and static Wasm facades already implement both, wired automatically from hover/focus.

NEW
- EditFile gains Bordered (wraps the field in a bordered card) and AllowDownload (file names become re-save links) -- matches Ant Design's already-uploaded-file card pattern.
- Table gains AriaLabel/ScrollRegionLabel/LoadingLabel/SelectRowLabelFor/FilterAppliedButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedLabel and keyboard row activation (Enter, WCAG 2.1.1); Pagination gains Disabled/AnnounceTotal.
- DatePicker/DateRangePicker: calendars are now real ARIA grids, FormatHintLabel, RTL-aware arrow keys, ArrowDown moves focus into the grid. Tabs also gain RTL-aware arrows.
- Alert/toasts gain SeverityLabel/CloseButtonLabel/Live localization; Popover/Popconfirm get aria-label fallbacks; Modal/Drawer inert their background while open (data-wss-keep-interactive escape hatch); tooltips gain full AT exposure + Escape-dismiss (WCAG 1.4.13).
- New --wss-color-primary-strong/--wss-color-error-strong tokens for AA text-on-fill contrast.

CHANGED
- --wss-color-text-deemphasized darkened to pass AA on hover; fixed control heights become min-height floors (WCAG 1.4.4) so a host page's own resets can't clamp them.

FIXED
- Table: Enter on interactive content in a plain Column no longer double-fires OnRowClick; a synthesized click during Loading no longer bypasses the same guard the keyboard path already had.
- Pickers: disabled calendar cells use aria-disabled instead of native disabled, so a run of disabled days can no longer trap or strand keyboard focus.

Full changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
